1nae|n|The fourth part; the quarter. ; The quarter of a circle, or of the circumference of a circle, an arc of 90¡, or one subtending a right angle at the center. ; One of the four parts into which a plane is divided by the coordinate axes. The upper right-hand part is the first quadrant; the upper left-hand part the second; the lower left-hand part the third; and the lower right-hand part the fourth quadrant. ; An instrument for measuring altitudes, variously constructed and mounted for different specific uses in astronomy, surveying, gunnery, etc., consisting commonly of a graduated arc of 90¡, with an index or vernier, and either plain or telescopic sights, and usually having a plumb line or spirit level for fixing the vertical or horizontal direction.	a:1m36,25,1;1qmx,12,3~1qmx,12,3;1m36,25,1	v:1ru6,19,9~1ru6,19,9	n:1qmx,6,2~1qmx,6,2	N:d40,72,6;1fse,69,4;ze8,32,3~d40,72,6;1fse,69,4;ze8,32,3
